  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HO-503001</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cyclone Mocha has affected 3.2m ppl; 1.6m ppl need lifesaving assistance in Myanmar. Rakhine State is the most affected w/ ppl facing multiple needs: 242K shelters were damaged; ppl lost basic HH &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; food items, &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; livelihoods; access to WASH services isbadly affected. Adolescent girls/women/kids/minorities/PWD &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; IDPs, already vulnerable pre-cyclone, now face increased risks due to loss of family/livelihoods. Females face SGBV &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; discrimination due to lack of privacy &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; hygienic sanitation to manage menstruation. Many cyclone survivors are seeking shelter in evacuation centers &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; monasteries after becoming homeless. Those who returned home must rebuild damaged houses w/ limited resources. Some markets have re-opened w/ soaring prices for (shelter) materials. Oxfam/partners RNA (17-21/5) shows widespread surface water contamination by fecal/solid wastes/leaves &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; saline waterwashed in by the cyclone. There&#x2019;s a need for clean drinking water/water treatment solutions. Sanitation facilities are damaged &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; repair/construction of latrines is needed for safe sanitation &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; to reduce risk of disease &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; GBV. Hygiene &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; dignity kits, &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; awareness sessions are needed to ensure personal hygiene &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; positive hygiene behavior incl. info on how to safely treat &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; store water, wash hands &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; avoid diarrhea, malaria &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; dengue fever. For ppl who&#x2019;ve lost everything, multipurpose cash is needed to meet their multiple needs &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; rebuild the local economy. UN flash appeal seeks $333 mil to provide lifesaving assistance to fill the gap. In Rakhine Oxfam will work in Sittwe &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Mrauk-U, priority 1 based on high needs &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; gaps; the target districts were in direct path of cyclone, so communities suffered up to 80-90% damage to shelter &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; productiveassets. Oxfam coordinated w/ DRA partners on ground &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; proposes WASH &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; MPC to reach 4530 HHs (22650 ppl; 52% F). We follow Cluster &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; SPHERE stds. in all activities &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; mainstream protection. Our partners were already working in the area &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; have good community access &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; rapport</narrative>
  </description>
